      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T20:38:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi VJ,\n\ni2c_port_to_ctrl[] can not be moved to mchp/i2c.c file, because each chip (mec170x, 152x and 172x) supports different number of i2c ports, there are not constant default ports for all chips, e.g. one chip support port 0, 1,2,3,4; but other chip support 0,2,3…\n\nbut “int board_i2c_p2c()” function can be moved to i2c.c, like this in i2c.c per your suggestion:\n\nextern const uint16_t i2c_port_to_ctrl[I2C_PORT_COUNT];\n__overridable int board_i2c_p2c(int port) {}\n\nIs this moving expected for you?\nneed your confirmation...",
      "parentUuid": "0df7c2ab_81beac24",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 183,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "172d3a25ca3c3519984b01e7cfb1535954304125",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
